      "value": {
        "title": "Whole-object gestures preserve camera, structure, scale and one-step Undo",
        "verify_smoke": [
          "AUTO-FEATURE-EDITING",
          "SMOKE-FEATURE-COPY-TRANSFORM"
        ],
        "owners": [
          "app",
          "maplib",
          "maplibui"
        ],
        "statement": "An explicit geometry editor tool consumes one-finger translation and two-finger rotation for every component and hole without scaling or moving the camera. Pointer transitions do not jump. Preview journals projected geometry without allocating history steps; one completed gesture allocates one Undo step. CANCEL restores the exact prior coordinates. History retains container and nested CRS so a transformed multipart geometry remains saveable after Undo/Redo. All editing actions stay inside the bottom panel without overflow.",
        "related_code": [
          "maplib/src/main/java/com/nextgis/maplib/util/GeometryTransform.java",
          "maplib/src/main/java/com/nextgis/maplib/map/GeometryTransformGesture.java",
          "maplibui/src/main/java/com/nextgis/maplibui/overlay/UndoRedoOverlay.java",
          "maplibui/src/main/java/com/nextgis/maplibui/fragment/BottomToolbar.java"
        ],
        "must_update_docs": [
          "docs/architecture/feature-copy-transform.md",
